{
  "video": {
    "id": "reYwbnuhFU0",
    "title": "Basic Mechanisms of Cloning, excerpt 2 | MIT 7.01SC Fundamentals of Biology",
    "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=reYwbnuhFU0",
    "channel": "MIT OpenCourseWare",
    "duration": 782,
    "language": "en"
  },
  "segment_count": 230,
  "segments": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "start": 6.71,
      "end": 10.77,
      "duration": 4.06,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: Now having cut DNA, we then need to"
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "start": 10.77,
      "end": 12.02,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "do something else."
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "start": 14.29,
      "end": 18.245,
      "duration": 3.955,
      "text": "What's the next thing we have to do?"
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "start": 18.245,
      "end": 19.71,
      "duration": 1.465,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: Paste it."
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "start": 19.71,
      "end": 21.29,
      "duration": 1.58,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: Paste it right."
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "start": 21.29,
      "end": 23.601,
      "duration": 2.311,
      "text": "Oh, I put past."
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "start": 23.601,
      "end": 25.84,
      "duration": 2.239,
      "text": "It should be paste."
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "start": 25.84,
      "end": 26.89,
      "duration": 1.05,
      "text": "There we go."
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "start": 26.89,
      "end": 28.68,
      "duration": 1.79,
      "text": "We should paste it."
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "start": 28.68,
      "end": 32.78,
      "duration": 4.1,
      "text": "So, how are we going to paste our DNA?"
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "start": 32.78,
      "end": 34.96,
      "duration": 2.18,
      "text": "So let's take some human DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "start": 39.02,
      "end": 41.36,
      "duration": 2.34,
      "text": "We'll take your human DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 12,
      "start": 41.36,
      "end": 43.49,
      "duration": 2.13,
      "text": "We'll add EcoR1 to it."
    },
    {
      "index": 13,
      "start": 43.49,
      "end": 48.87,
      "duration": 5.38,
      "text": "And your human DNA is going to get cut up in lots of little"
    },
    {
      "index": 14,
      "start": 48.87,
      "end": 52.68,
      "duration": 3.81,
      "text": "pieces of length about 4,000."
    },
    {
      "index": 15,
      "start": 52.68,
      "end": 56.42,
      "duration": 3.74,
      "text": "And I'm writing R1 at the ends because these pieces of DNA"
    },
    {
      "index": 16,
      "start": 56.42,
      "end": 59.23,
      "duration": 2.81,
      "text": "have EcoR1 sites."
    },
    {
      "index": 17,
      "start": 59.23,
      "end": 65.79,
      "duration": 6.56,
      "text": "Now, I can take that human DNA and I can combine it with"
    },
    {
      "index": 18,
      "start": 65.79,
      "end": 67.04,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "other pieces of DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 19,
      "start": 71.27,
      "end": 72.71,
      "duration": 1.44,
      "text": "Here's a piece of DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 20,
      "start": 72.71,
      "end": 76.5,
      "duration": 3.79,
      "text": "Remember it had this overhang like that."
    },
    {
      "index": 21,
      "start": 79.9,
      "end": 85.41,
      "duration": 5.51,
      "text": "T-T-A-A was this piece here of human DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 22,
      "start": 89.42,
      "end": 94.51,
      "duration": 5.09,
      "text": "And I could take another piece of DNA that matched it a"
    },
    {
      "index": 23,
      "start": 94.51,
      "end": 101.1,
      "duration": 6.59,
      "text": "A-A-T-T."
    },
    {
      "index": 24,
      "start": 101.1,
      "end": 102.29,
      "duration": 1.19,
      "text": "And it doesn't have to be human."
    },
    {
      "index": 25,
      "start": 102.29,
      "end": 104.08,
      "duration": 1.79,
      "text": "It could be something else."
    },
    {
      "index": 26,
      "start": 104.08,
      "end": 105.33,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "It could be zebra."
    },
    {
      "index": 27,
      "start": 107.66,
      "end": 113.32,
      "duration": 5.66,
      "text": "Some human DNA, some zebra DNA, and by that base pairing"
    },
    {
      "index": 28,
      "start": 113.32,
      "end": 117.732,
      "duration": 4.412,
      "text": "of those four bases, they'll sort of stick."
    },
    {
      "index": 29,
      "start": 117.732,
      "end": 118.58,
      "duration": 0.848,
      "text": "It's not that strong."
    },
    {
      "index": 30,
      "start": 118.58,
      "end": 121.536,
      "duration": 2.956,
      "text": "It's four bases of base pairing, but they'll stick."
    },
    {
      "index": 31,
      "start": 121.536,
      "end": 125.1,
      "duration": 3.564,
      "text": "Now I'd like to glue them together."
    },
    {
      "index": 32,
      "start": 125.1,
      "end": 128.889,
      "duration": 3.789,
      "text": "What's the word for attaching together DNA strands?"
    },
    {
      "index": 33,
      "start": 128.889,
      "end": 130.5,
      "duration": 1.611,
      "text": "We talked about it--"
    },
    {
      "index": 34,
      "start": 130.5,
      "end": 135.01,
      "duration": 4.51,
      "text": "Ligate, we want to ligate them together."
    },
    {
      "index": 35,
      "start": 135.01,
      "end": 137.75,
      "duration": 2.74,
      "text": "So now we go back to our MIT engineers and say, please"
    },
    {
      "index": 36,
      "start": 137.75,
      "end": 140.15,
      "duration": 2.4,
      "text": "invent me a protein that's able to ligate"
    },
    {
      "index": 37,
      "start": 140.15,
      "end": 142.85,
      "duration": 2.7,
      "text": "together pieces of DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 38,
      "start": 142.85,
      "end": 146.72,
      "duration": 3.87,
      "text": "But actually, who invented it first?"
    },
    {
      "index": 39,
      "start": 146.72,
      "end": 148.22,
      "duration": 1.5,
      "text": "Bacteria invented it first."
    },
    {
      "index": 40,
      "start": 148.22,
      "end": 150.26,
      "duration": 2.04,
      "text": "And it's called?"
    },
    {
      "index": 41,
      "start": 150.26,
      "end": 151.62,
      "duration": 1.36,
      "text": "Ligase."
    },
    {
      "index": 42,
      "start": 151.62,
      "end": 154.11,
      "duration": 2.49,
      "text": "So all we have to do is add ligase."
    },
    {
      "index": 43,
      "start": 154.11,
      "end": 155.45,
      "duration": 1.34,
      "text": "So it was kind of useful to know how"
    },
    {
      "index": 44,
      "start": 155.45,
      "end": 157.18,
      "duration": 1.73,
      "text": "DNA replication worked."
    },
    {
      "index": 45,
      "start": 157.18,
      "end": 160.11,
      "duration": 2.93,
      "text": "We add ligase."
    },
    {
      "index": 46,
      "start": 160.11,
      "end": 164.26,
      "duration": 4.15,
      "text": "And what does ligase do for a living?"
    },
    {
      "index": 47,
      "start": 164.26,
      "end": 168.23,
      "duration": 3.97,
      "text": "For a living, ligase is paid to go around and find pieces"
    },
    {
      "index": 48,
      "start": 168.23,
      "end": 172.89,
      "duration": 4.66,
      "text": "of DNA that have nicks and seal them back up by repairing"
    },
    {
      "index": 49,
      "start": 172.89,
      "end": 174.86,
      "duration": 1.97,
      "text": "the sugar phosphate backbone of DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 50,
      "start": 178.48,
      "end": 183.7,
      "duration": 5.22,
      "text": "And again, ancient molecular biologists would prove their"
    },
    {
      "index": 51,
      "start": 183.7,
      "end": 188.09,
      "duration": 4.39,
      "text": "mettle by purifying ligase and using it in their reactions."
    },
    {
      "index": 52,
      "start": 188.09,
      "end": 191.48,
      "duration": 3.39,
      "text": "And today, where do we get ligase?"
    },
    {
      "index": 53,
      "start": 191.48,
      "end": 193.1,
      "duration": 1.62,
      "text": "It's in the catalog."
    },
    {
      "index": 54,
      "start": 193.1,
      "end": 196.76,
      "duration": 3.66,
      "text": "Ligase is in the catalog, reasonably cheap."
    },
    {
      "index": 55,
      "start": 196.76,
      "end": 204.77,
      "duration": 8.01,
      "text": "So, when we add ligase we could now get a hybrid piece"
    },
    {
      "index": 56,
      "start": 204.77,
      "end": 208.31,
      "duration": 3.54,
      "text": "of DNA that was half human and half zebra."
    },
    {
      "index": 57,
      "start": 208.31,
      "end": 210.95,
      "duration": 2.64,
      "text": "I got to say, this freaks some people out."
    },
    {
      "index": 58,
      "start": 210.95,
      "end": 214.61,
      "duration": 3.66,
      "text": "This doesn't freak me out because it's just a sequence"
    },
    {
      "index": 59,
      "start": 214.61,
      "end": 215.41,
      "duration": 0.8,
      "text": "of nucleotides."
    },
    {
      "index": 60,
      "start": 215.41,
      "end": 217.92,
      "duration": 2.51,
      "text": "If I give you a sequence of nucleotides, to my mind,"
    },
    {
      "index": 61,
      "start": 217.92,
      "end": 220.99,
      "duration": 3.07,
      "text": "there's nothing human or zebra about it."
    },
    {
      "index": 62,
      "start": 220.99,
      "end": 222.39,
      "duration": 1.4,
      "text": "It's a chemical."
    },
    {
      "index": 63,
      "start": 222.39,
      "end": 226.21,
      "duration": 3.82,
      "text": "And you can make bonds between chemicals and all that."
    },
    {
      "index": 64,
      "start": 226.21,
      "end": 232.08,
      "duration": 5.87,
      "text": "So, we now pasted our DNA using ligase."
    },
    {
      "index": 65,
      "start": 232.08,
      "end": 234.07,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "Ligase from the catalog."
    },
    {
      "index": 66,
      "start": 234.07,
      "end": 238.55,
      "duration": 4.48,
      "text": "Now the question is, what are we going to paste our DNA to?"
    },
    {
      "index": 67,
      "start": 241.4,
      "end": 243.185,
      "duration": 1.785,
      "text": "What do we paste our DNA to?"
    },
    {
      "index": 68,
      "start": 253.84,
      "end": 260.91,
      "duration": 7.07,
      "text": "We're going to paste our DNA to a fascinating other piece"
    },
    {
      "index": 69,
      "start": 260.91,
      "end": 269.224,
      "duration": 8.314,
      "text": "of DNA like this."
    },
    {
      "index": 70,
      "start": 269.224,
      "end": 273.4,
      "duration": 4.176,
      "text": "I'll make that a little bigger here."
    },
    {
      "index": 71,
      "start": 273.4,
      "end": 278.58,
      "duration": 5.18,
      "text": "That has an EcoR1 site, has an EcoR1 site."
    },
    {
      "index": 72,
      "start": 278.58,
      "end": 288.68,
      "duration": 10.1,
      "text": "And we're going to take our human DNA and paste it in such"
    },
    {
      "index": 73,
      "start": 288.68,
      "end": 290.89,
      "duration": 2.21,
      "text": "a way that it makes a circle."
    },
    {
      "index": 74,
      "start": 290.89,
      "end": 295.9,
      "duration": 5.01,
      "text": "This piece of DNA is a vector."
    },
    {
      "index": 75,
      "start": 295.9,
      "end": 297.47,
      "duration": 1.57,
      "text": "Vector means it travels around."
    },
    {
      "index": 76,
      "start": 297.47,
      "end": 299.7,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "It carries things with it."
    },
    {
      "index": 77,
      "start": 299.7,
      "end": 311.84,
      "duration": 12.14,
      "text": "So I want this vector to be able to replicate if I"
    },
    {
      "index": 78,
      "start": 311.84,
      "end": 313.99,
      "duration": 2.15,
      "text": "transfer it to E Coli."
    },
    {
      "index": 79,
      "start": 313.99,
      "end": 314.81,
      "duration": 0.82,
      "text": "So that's the trick."
    },
    {
      "index": 80,
      "start": 314.81,
      "end": 317.25,
      "duration": 2.44,
      "text": "I would like to be able to attachment my human DNA to"
    },
    {
      "index": 81,
      "start": 317.25,
      "end": 320.72,
      "duration": 3.47,
      "text": "this vector DNA, and when I transfer it to E coli, have"
    },
    {
      "index": 82,
      "start": 320.72,
      "end": 322.45,
      "duration": 1.73,
      "text": "this thing be able to grow."
    },
    {
      "index": 83,
      "start": 322.45,
      "end": 327.46,
      "duration": 5.01,
      "text": "So that means we need to invent a piece of DNA, a"
    },
    {
      "index": 84,
      "start": 327.46,
      "end": 332.01,
      "duration": 4.55,
      "text": "vector, that is capable of causing E. coli"
    },
    {
      "index": 85,
      "start": 332.01,
      "end": 334.45,
      "duration": 2.44,
      "text": "to replicate itself."
    },
    {
      "index": 86,
      "start": 334.45,
      "end": 338.51,
      "duration": 4.06,
      "text": "It's got to have all the instructions to cause E. coli"
    },
    {
      "index": 87,
      "start": 338.51,
      "end": 342.28,
      "duration": 3.77,
      "text": "to replicate this piece of DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 88,
      "start": 342.28,
      "end": 346.92,
      "duration": 4.64,
      "text": "So this is another amazing bit of engineering."
    },
    {
      "index": 89,
      "start": 346.92,
      "end": 351.65,
      "duration": 4.73,
      "text": "How do we invent just the right sequence of letters that"
    },
    {
      "index": 90,
      "start": 351.65,
      "end": 353.99,
      "duration": 2.34,
      "text": "would allow E. coli to replicate this thing?"
    },
    {
      "index": 91,
      "start": 353.99,
      "end": 355.75,
      "duration": 1.76,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: Already been invented."
    },
    {
      "index": 92,
      "start": 355.75,
      "end": 356.63,
      "duration": 0.88,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: Sorry."
    },
    {
      "index": 93,
      "start": 356.63,
      "end": 359.03,
      "duration": 2.4,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: It's already been invented by E. coli."
    },
    {
      "index": 94,
      "start": 359.03,
      "end": 361.49,
      "duration": 2.46,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: It's already been invented by E."
    },
    {
      "index": 95,
      "start": 361.49,
      "end": 363.61,
      "duration": 2.12,
      "text": "coli, hasn't it?"
    },
    {
      "index": 96,
      "start": 363.61,
      "end": 367.79,
      "duration": 4.18,
      "text": "So you're getting the theme here, is that we don't"
    },
    {
      "index": 97,
      "start": 367.79,
      "end": 370.01,
      "duration": 2.22,
      "text": "actually do anything in molecular biology."
    },
    {
      "index": 98,
      "start": 373.48,
      "end": 376.83,
      "duration": 3.35,
      "text": "Now look, in fairness, life's had 3.5 billion years."
    },
    {
      "index": 99,
      "start": 376.83,
      "end": 379.34,
      "duration": 2.51,
      "text": "We've been at this a decade or two, on the"
    },
    {
      "index": 100,
      "start": 379.34,
      "end": 380.79,
      "duration": 1.45,
      "text": "whole, maybe three."
    },
    {
      "index": 101,
      "start": 380.79,
      "end": 383.08,
      "duration": 2.29,
      "text": "On the whole, life's had a lot more time to"
    },
    {
      "index": 102,
      "start": 383.08,
      "end": 384.09,
      "duration": 1.01,
      "text": "work this stuff out."
    },
    {
      "index": 103,
      "start": 384.09,
      "end": 387.36,
      "duration": 3.27,
      "text": "And usually the best solution is to look in nature to see"
    },
    {
      "index": 104,
      "start": 387.36,
      "end": 390.42,
      "duration": 3.06,
      "text": "where nature has already done it for you."
    },
    {
      "index": 105,
      "start": 390.42,
      "end": 395.67,
      "duration": 5.25,
      "text": "So E. coli, it turns out, replicates its own chromosome."
    },
    {
      "index": 106,
      "start": 395.67,
      "end": 399.01,
      "duration": 3.34,
      "text": "You could use the machinery from its own chromosome."
    },
    {
      "index": 107,
      "start": 399.01,
      "end": 401.13,
      "duration": 2.12,
      "text": "But it turns out even better than that."
    },
    {
      "index": 108,
      "start": 401.13,
      "end": 405.23,
      "duration": 4.1,
      "text": "E. coli has the following."
    },
    {
      "index": 109,
      "start": 408.71,
      "end": 411.57,
      "duration": 2.86,
      "text": "Here's its big chromosome, four million letters of E."
    },
    {
      "index": 110,
      "start": 411.57,
      "end": 413.79,
      "duration": 2.22,
      "text": "coli chromosome."
    },
    {
      "index": 111,
      "start": 413.79,
      "end": 420.1,
      "duration": 6.31,
      "text": "E. Coli also has within it little circles"
    },
    {
      "index": 112,
      "start": 420.1,
      "end": 423.08,
      "duration": 2.98,
      "text": "of DNA called plasmids."
    },
    {
      "index": 113,
      "start": 427.59,
      "end": 430.37,
      "duration": 2.78,
      "text": "These little circles of DNA are able to"
    },
    {
      "index": 114,
      "start": 430.37,
      "end": 432.02,
      "duration": 1.65,
      "text": "autonomously replicate."
    },
    {
      "index": 115,
      "start": 432.02,
      "end": 433.33,
      "duration": 1.31,
      "text": "They can copy themselves."
    },
    {
      "index": 116,
      "start": 433.33,
      "end": 437.18,
      "duration": 3.85,
      "text": "Or that is to say, E. coli copies them."
    },
    {
      "index": 117,
      "start": 437.18,
      "end": 441.31,
      "duration": 4.13,
      "text": "These little plasmids have the full replication instructions"
    },
    {
      "index": 118,
      "start": 441.31,
      "end": 442.48,
      "duration": 1.17,
      "text": "encoded in them."
    },
    {
      "index": 119,
      "start": 442.48,
      "end": 444.45,
      "duration": 1.97,
      "text": "Now why does E. coli have these plasmids?"
    },
    {
      "index": 120,
      "start": 444.45,
      "end": 445.53,
      "duration": 1.08,
      "text": "What's in these plasmids?"
    },
    {
      "index": 121,
      "start": 445.53,
      "end": 447.22,
      "duration": 1.69,
      "text": "What's going on?"
    },
    {
      "index": 122,
      "start": 447.22,
      "end": 449.05,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "Well let's blow up one of these plasmids."
    },
    {
      "index": 123,
      "start": 451.86,
      "end": 454.37,
      "duration": 2.51,
      "text": "It's a big circle."
    },
    {
      "index": 124,
      "start": 454.37,
      "end": 460.96,
      "duration": 6.59,
      "text": "And it has an instruction here, a sequence, called an"
    },
    {
      "index": 125,
      "start": 460.96,
      "end": 471.195,
      "duration": 10.235,
      "text": "origin of replication - or amongst friends, just ORI."
    },
    {
      "index": 126,
      "start": 471.195,
      "end": 472.48,
      "duration": 1.285,
      "text": "It's called ORI."
    },
    {
      "index": 127,
      "start": 472.48,
      "end": 475.85,
      "duration": 3.37,
      "text": "You'll find on maps, origin of replication."
    },
    {
      "index": 128,
      "start": 475.85,
      "end": 479.82,
      "duration": 3.97,
      "text": "That sequence alone is enough to cause E. coli to open it up"
    },
    {
      "index": 129,
      "start": 479.82,
      "end": 484.33,
      "duration": 4.51,
      "text": "and start doing its DNA replication from the origin."
    },
    {
      "index": 130,
      "start": 484.33,
      "end": 489.52,
      "duration": 5.19,
      "text": "But what tells you why this is so important is that these"
    },
    {
      "index": 131,
      "start": 489.52,
      "end": 496.16,
      "duration": 6.64,
      "text": "plasmids typically have one or two genes."
    },
    {
      "index": 132,
      "start": 496.16,
      "end": 501.15,
      "duration": 4.99,
      "text": "And the one or two genes that they typically have are genes"
    },
    {
      "index": 133,
      "start": 501.15,
      "end": 509.33,
      "duration": 8.18,
      "text": "that encode a protein that gives them resistance to an"
    },
    {
      "index": 134,
      "start": 509.33,
      "end": 515.424,
      "duration": 6.094,
      "text": "antibiotic, like say, penicillin."
    },
    {
      "index": 135,
      "start": 519.75,
      "end": 522.2,
      "duration": 2.45,
      "text": "There could be a gene that gives you penicillin"
    },
    {
      "index": 136,
      "start": 522.2,
      "end": 523.45,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "resistance."
    },
    {
      "index": 137,
      "start": 526.07,
      "end": 527.07,
      "duration": 1.0,
      "text": "That's kind of cool."
    },
    {
      "index": 138,
      "start": 527.07,
      "end": 529.14,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "E. coli, or other bacteria--"
    },
    {
      "index": 139,
      "start": 529.14,
      "end": 531.23,
      "duration": 2.09,
      "text": "not E. coli necessarily for penicillin--"
    },
    {
      "index": 140,
      "start": 531.23,
      "end": 534.52,
      "duration": 3.29,
      "text": "carry around often little circles."
    },
    {
      "index": 141,
      "start": 534.52,
      "end": 536.5,
      "duration": 1.98,
      "text": "And these little circles encode genes that give them"
    },
    {
      "index": 142,
      "start": 536.5,
      "end": 541.54,
      "duration": 5.04,
      "text": "resistance to streptomycin, penicillin, ampicillin, all"
    },
    {
      "index": 143,
      "start": 541.54,
      "end": 542.79,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "sorts of things."
    },
    {
      "index": 144,
      "start": 546.37,
      "end": 550.36,
      "duration": 3.99,
      "text": "This allows it to grow, even if you're taking penicillin."
    },
    {
      "index": 145,
      "start": 553.45,
      "end": 555.84,
      "duration": 2.39,
      "text": "Now, that's pretty clever."
    },
    {
      "index": 146,
      "start": 555.84,
      "end": 558.09,
      "duration": 2.25,
      "text": "How did E. Coli come up?"
    },
    {
      "index": 147,
      "start": 558.09,
      "end": 561.98,
      "duration": 3.89,
      "text": "How is it so smart to know to have come up with a gene able"
    },
    {
      "index": 148,
      "start": 561.98,
      "end": 564.67,
      "duration": 2.69,
      "text": "to break down penicillin, given that we've only been"
    },
    {
      "index": 149,
      "start": 564.67,
      "end": 569.62,
      "duration": 4.95,
      "text": "using penicillin since the 1940s?"
    },
    {
      "index": 150,
      "start": 569.62,
      "end": 572.51,
      "duration": 2.89,
      "text": "Pretty fast for E. coli to have figured out how to do"
    },
    {
      "index": 151,
      "start": 572.51,
      "end": 573.76,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "that, isn't it?"
    },
    {
      "index": 152,
      "start": 579.02,
      "end": 582.9,
      "duration": 3.88,
      "text": "Oh yeah, who invented penicillin?"
    },
    {
      "index": 153,
      "start": 582.9,
      "end": 584.44,
      "duration": 1.54,
      "text": "Nature invented penicillin."
    },
    {
      "index": 154,
      "start": 584.44,
      "end": 586.78,
      "duration": 2.34,
      "text": "It's produced by fungi."
    },
    {
      "index": 155,
      "start": 586.78,
      "end": 590.25,
      "duration": 3.47,
      "text": "Fungi have been fighting E. Coli with penicillin for"
    },
    {
      "index": 156,
      "start": 590.25,
      "end": 592.07,
      "duration": 1.82,
      "text": "millions of years."
    },
    {
      "index": 157,
      "start": 592.07,
      "end": 595.185,
      "duration": 3.115,
      "text": "E. coli didn't invent it for us."
    },
    {
      "index": 158,
      "start": 595.185,
      "end": 598.69,
      "duration": 3.505,
      "text": "E. Coli invented it because it's in a war down there at"
    },
    {
      "index": 159,
      "start": 598.69,
      "end": 601.46,
      "duration": 2.77,
      "text": "the single cell level with fungi."
    },
    {
      "index": 160,
      "start": 601.46,
      "end": 602.85,
      "duration": 1.39,
      "text": "Fungi make antibi--"
    },
    {
      "index": 161,
      "start": 602.85,
      "end": 604.73,
      "duration": 1.88,
      "text": "You see, we think we're so cool."
    },
    {
      "index": 162,
      "start": 604.73,
      "end": 606.16,
      "duration": 1.43,
      "text": "We make antibiotics."
    },
    {
      "index": 163,
      "start": 606.16,
      "end": 607.5,
      "duration": 1.34,
      "text": "Well we've been making antibiotics"
    },
    {
      "index": 164,
      "start": 607.5,
      "end": 609.64,
      "duration": 2.14,
      "text": "only since the 1940s."
    },
    {
      "index": 165,
      "start": 609.64,
      "end": 612.35,
      "duration": 2.71,
      "text": "Nature's been making antibiotics forever."
    },
    {
      "index": 166,
      "start": 612.35,
      "end": 615.27,
      "duration": 2.92,
      "text": "Just like the viruses are infecting E. coli and E. coli"
    },
    {
      "index": 167,
      "start": 615.27,
      "end": 617.77,
      "duration": 2.5,
      "text": "needs an immune system against the viruses."
    },
    {
      "index": 168,
      "start": 617.77,
      "end": 621.15,
      "duration": 3.38,
      "text": "Well the fungi are throwing antibiotics at the bacteria"
    },
    {
      "index": 169,
      "start": 621.15,
      "end": 622.62,
      "duration": 1.47,
      "text": "and it needs a defense mechanism."
    },
    {
      "index": 170,
      "start": 622.62,
      "end": 625.57,
      "duration": 2.95,
      "text": "And the defense mechanism are these genes that can break"
    },
    {
      "index": 171,
      "start": 625.57,
      "end": 628.14,
      "duration": 2.57,
      "text": "down those antibiotics."
    },
    {
      "index": 172,
      "start": 628.14,
      "end": 630.04,
      "duration": 1.9,
      "text": "And as usual, we just come along and we"
    },
    {
      "index": 173,
      "start": 630.04,
      "end": 631.86,
      "duration": 1.82,
      "text": "say, oh look at that."
    },
    {
      "index": 174,
      "start": 631.86,
      "end": 633.02,
      "duration": 1.16,
      "text": "It's already been invented."
    },
    {
      "index": 175,
      "start": 633.02,
      "end": 633.61,
      "duration": 0.59,
      "text": "Kind of cool."
    },
    {
      "index": 176,
      "start": 633.61,
      "end": 636.87,
      "duration": 3.26,
      "text": "We'll use that one too."
    },
    {
      "index": 177,
      "start": 636.87,
      "end": 638.37,
      "duration": 1.5,
      "text": "Now why are these on these little circles?"
    },
    {
      "index": 178,
      "start": 638.37,
      "end": 642.75,
      "duration": 4.38,
      "text": "They're on the little circles because when this bacteria has"
    },
    {
      "index": 179,
      "start": 642.75,
      "end": 647.42,
      "duration": 4.67,
      "text": "lived a long and happy life and it dies and it spews its"
    },
    {
      "index": 180,
      "start": 647.42,
      "end": 656.54,
      "duration": 9.12,
      "text": "guts out, neighboring bacteria suck up the DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 181,
      "start": 656.54,
      "end": 659.67,
      "duration": 3.13,
      "text": "Sounds a little cannibalistic or something."
    },
    {
      "index": 182,
      "start": 659.67,
      "end": 661.28,
      "duration": 1.61,
      "text": "But that's how it is down there at"
    },
    {
      "index": 183,
      "start": 661.28,
      "end": 662.88,
      "duration": 1.6,
      "text": "the single cell level."
    },
    {
      "index": 184,
      "start": 662.88,
      "end": 665.42,
      "duration": 2.54,
      "text": "The neighboring bacteria will suck up DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 185,
      "start": 665.42,
      "end": 666.98,
      "duration": 1.56,
      "text": "And why is that cool?"
    },
    {
      "index": 186,
      "start": 666.98,
      "end": 671.31,
      "duration": 4.33,
      "text": "It's cool because they can acquire these resistances."
    },
    {
      "index": 187,
      "start": 671.31,
      "end": 672.25,
      "duration": 0.94,
      "text": "That's pretty impressive."
    },
    {
      "index": 188,
      "start": 672.25,
      "end": 673.67,
      "duration": 1.42,
      "text": "They can acquire the resistance."
    },
    {
      "index": 189,
      "start": 673.67,
      "end": 676.89,
      "duration": 3.22,
      "text": "And in fact, it even works across species."
    },
    {
      "index": 190,
      "start": 676.89,
      "end": 678.49,
      "duration": 1.6,
      "text": "That's why you don't put it on the chromosome here."
    },
    {
      "index": 191,
      "start": 678.49,
      "end": 681.14,
      "duration": 2.65,
      "text": "Because E. coli could pick it up from another species that's"
    },
    {
      "index": 192,
      "start": 681.14,
      "end": 683.16,
      "duration": 2.02,
      "text": "not E. coli, but related enough that it"
    },
    {
      "index": 193,
      "start": 683.16,
      "end": 684.16,
      "duration": 1.0,
      "text": "can use that plasmid."
    },
    {
      "index": 194,
      "start": 684.16,
      "end": 688.64,
      "duration": 4.48,
      "text": "And you can transfer antibiotic resistance across"
    },
    {
      "index": 195,
      "start": 688.64,
      "end": 692.41,
      "duration": 3.77,
      "text": "many species of bacteria."
    },
    {
      "index": 196,
      "start": 692.41,
      "end": 696.52,
      "duration": 4.11,
      "text": "So the bacteria like to suck up DNA and see what they find."
    },
    {
      "index": 197,
      "start": 696.52,
      "end": 698.56,
      "duration": 2.04,
      "text": "Pretty cool."
    },
    {
      "index": 198,
      "start": 698.56,
      "end": 701.07,
      "duration": 2.51,
      "text": "By the way, this is also why indiscriminate use of"
    },
    {
      "index": 199,
      "start": 701.07,
      "end": 704.56,
      "duration": 3.49,
      "text": "antibiotics, for example, in animal feed, or when you were"
    },
    {
      "index": 200,
      "start": 704.56,
      "end": 707.67,
      "duration": 3.11,
      "text": "given antibiotics by the MIT health service and are told to"
    },
    {
      "index": 201,
      "start": 707.67,
      "end": 710.69,
      "duration": 3.02,
      "text": "take them for two weeks and you take them for five days,"
    },
    {
      "index": 202,
      "start": 710.69,
      "end": 712.26,
      "duration": 1.57,
      "text": "you're not doing anything very good."
    },
    {
      "index": 203,
      "start": 712.26,
      "end": 715.98,
      "duration": 3.72,
      "text": "You're just selecting for bacteria that can grow in the"
    },
    {
      "index": 204,
      "start": 715.98,
      "end": 719.21,
      "duration": 3.23,
      "text": "presence of antibiotics and selecting for multidrug"
    },
    {
      "index": 205,
      "start": 719.21,
      "end": 721.47,
      "duration": 2.26,
      "text": "resistance in the spread of antibiotics."
    },
    {
      "index": 206,
      "start": 721.47,
      "end": 722.41,
      "duration": 0.94,
      "text": "We have to be pretty careful."
    },
    {
      "index": 207,
      "start": 722.41,
      "end": 725.56,
      "duration": 3.15,
      "text": "Because all these mechanisms of swapping antibiotic"
    },
    {
      "index": 208,
      "start": 725.56,
      "end": 728.46,
      "duration": 2.9,
      "text": "resistance are pretty impressive tricks."
    },
    {
      "index": 209,
      "start": 728.46,
      "end": 730.32,
      "duration": 1.86,
      "text": "Anyway, so these things exist."
    },
    {
      "index": 210,
      "start": 730.32,
      "end": 732.57,
      "duration": 2.25,
      "text": "And originally, molecular biologists"
    },
    {
      "index": 211,
      "start": 732.57,
      "end": 734.05,
      "duration": 1.48,
      "text": "discovered these plasmids."
    },
    {
      "index": 212,
      "start": 734.05,
      "end": 735.68,
      "duration": 1.63,
      "text": "They purified these plasmids."
    },
    {
      "index": 213,
      "start": 735.68,
      "end": 737.46,
      "duration": 1.78,
      "text": "And the deal was this, they cut the"
    },
    {
      "index": 214,
      "start": 737.46,
      "end": 742.62,
      "duration": 5.16,
      "text": "plasmid with EcoR1, ideally."
    },
    {
      "index": 215,
      "start": 742.62,
      "end": 745.98,
      "duration": 3.36,
      "text": "So I'm going to put this up here, vectors."
    },
    {
      "index": 216,
      "start": 745.98,
      "end": 747.34,
      "duration": 1.36,
      "text": "They cut the plasmid with EcoR1."
    },
    {
      "index": 217,
      "start": 751.8,
      "end": 757.06,
      "duration": 5.26,
      "text": "They ligate human DNA into it."
    },
    {
      "index": 218,
      "start": 757.06,
      "end": 758.64,
      "duration": 1.58,
      "text": "And they get these circles."
    },
    {
      "index": 219,
      "start": 758.64,
      "end": 761.64,
      "duration": 3.0,
      "text": "And there you go."
    },
    {
      "index": 220,
      "start": 761.64,
      "end": 768.2,
      "duration": 6.56,
      "text": "Now today, obviously, if I wanted to do this experiment,"
    },
    {
      "index": 221,
      "start": 768.2,
      "end": 772.16,
      "duration": 3.96,
      "text": "would I purify the plasmid myself?"
    },
    {
      "index": 222,
      "start": 772.16,
      "end": 772.54,
      "duration": 0.38,
      "text": "No."
    },
    {
      "index": 223,
      "start": 772.54,
      "end": 774.1,
      "duration": 1.56,
      "text": "Where would I get the plasmid from?"
    },
    {
      "index": 224,
      "start": 774.1,
      "end": 774.92,
      "duration": 0.82,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: Catalog."
    },
    {
      "index": 225,
      "start": 774.92,
      "end": 775.98,
      "duration": 1.06,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: It's in the catalog."
    },
    {
      "index": 226,
      "start": 775.98,
      "end": 777.66,
      "duration": 1.68,
      "text": "There's a whole section a plasmids here."
    },
    {
      "index": 227,
      "start": 777.66,
      "end": 779.24,
      "duration": 1.58,
      "text": "They have vectors of all sorts."
    },
    {
      "index": 228,
      "start": 779.24,
      "end": 781.31,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "So you get it from the catalog."
    },
    {
      "index": 229,
      "start": 781.31,
      "end": 782.56,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "All right."
    }
  ],
  "course": {
    "category": "Biology & Chemistry",
    "title": "Introduction to Biology",
    "source_url": "https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLF83B8D8C87426E44"
  }
}